.TH BZIP2 1
.SH NAME
bzip2, bunzip2 \- block-sorting compression and decompression utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bzip2
[
.B \-cdkv
] [
.BI \- level
] [
.IR file ...
]
.br
.B bunzip2
[
.B \-ck
] [
.IR file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Bzip2
and
.B bunzip2
perform data compression and decompression
compatible with the Unix
.I bzip2
file format,
which combines a Burrows-Wheeler block-sorting transform
with a move-to-front coder, two run-length encoding passes,
and an adaptive Huffman coder.
If no arguments are given
.B bzip2
compresses each
.I file
replacing it by a file of the same
name with the
.B .bz2
suffix appended.
If no files are given, standard input
and standard output are used.
.I Level
is a single decimal digit between 1 and 9;
it selects a block size of
.IR level " * 100000"
bytes.
Higher numbers normally give better compression at the cost of
more memory and time.
The default
.I level
is 9.
The
.B \-v
option causes
.B bzip2
to report the compression ratio of each file that
it compresses.
The
.B \-c
option writes the compressed data to standard output and
leaves the input file unchanged.
The
.B \-k
option keeps (does not delete) the input file.
The
.B \-d
option requests decompression and is equivalent to running
.BR bunzip2 .
.PP
.B Bunzip2
performs the opposite operation to
.BR bzip2 ;
each
.I file
(which must have a
.BR .bz2 ,
.BR .tbz
or
.B .tbz2
suffix) is uncompressed, and replaced
by a file of the same name with the
.B .bz2
suffix removed (or, for
.B .tbz
and
.BR .tbz2 ,
replaced with
.BR .tar ).
If no files are given,
standard input and standard output are used.
The
.B \-c
option writes the decompressed data to standard output and
leaves the input file unchanged.
The
.B \-k
option keeps (does not delete) the input
.B .bz2
file.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/bzip2.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/bunzip2.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR gzip (1),
.IR filter (2),
.IR filter-deflate (2)
.SH BUGS
This compressor emits a single Huffman table per block (the spec
allows 2 to 6), which gives correct, well-formed output but worse
compression on heterogeneous inputs than GNU
.IR bzip2 .
.br
The BWT sort is a 3-way multikey quicksort with a bucket pre-pass;
it is correct but slower than libbzip2's own sorter. For very
large block sizes
.RB ( "-8" ", " "-9" )
on highly repetitive input the time grows accordingly; use a
smaller block size if needed.
